KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ called: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ deduced: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
decltype(invoke()) in a static data member's initializer, where invoke
calls a member template with a deduced return type, is not int while the
class is instantiated ("template 'element' not found"; assertion 2 fails).
GCC 11's std::visit (cpp17_visit_libstdcxx) has this shape (_S_apply's
decltype(__visit_invoke(...)) in __gen_vtable's static _S_vtable) and drops
declval<decltype()>; not confirmed to be the same cause.
